ntation and can be constrained with explicit provider selection.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill persists caches, extracted page text, provider state, and routing receipts under the cache directory, with documented disable and clear controls; this is purpose-aligned local state, not hidden system persistence.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill purpose, entrypoints, provider implementations, routing logic, extraction code, and helper modules are coherent with a multi-provider web search and extraction tool.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable with search queries and extraction URLs being sent to the selected third-party providers. For sensitive work, choose a provider explicitly or use a self-hosted SearXNG instance, use --no-cache or WSP_DISABLE_CACHE=1 when needed, and protect any config.json or .env file containing API keys.","findings":"[PE3] expected: The .env reference is setup guidance for provider API keys in a provider-integration skill, not evidence of arbitrary credential-file access or theft.\n[TP4] expected: The repeated mismatch findings appear to evaluate individual support modules in isolation; the inspected artifact as a whole includes the advertised search, provider routing, extraction, caching, setup, and safety components.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1791628449927}}}}}